# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout converts everything to CRLF, and the
# result is not merely cosmetic: `docker-entrypoint.sh` ends up in the production
# image with a `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang, which the kernel cannot resolve. The
# container then dies at startup with
#
#     exec /usr/local/bin/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# - a message that names the file it just found, and says nothing about carriage
# returns. The Linux deploy host never reproduces it, because git checks out LF
# there, so the image is only broken when built from a Windows working copy.
#
# `* text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository. The explicit `eol=lf` entries
# below additionally force LF in the WORKING TREE, which is what matters for files
# that are executed by something other than Windows: shell scripts, anything
# COPYed into a Linux image, and Python that a Linux interpreter runs.

* text=auto

# Executed by /bin/sh inside Linux containers, or by the deploy host.
*.sh            text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
nginx/*.conf    text eol=lf

# Run by CPython inside the container. A shebang is not the issue here, but a
# consistent representation keeps hashes and line offsets stable, and the turtle
# shim's line-offset arithmetic depends on counting newlines.
*.py            text eol=lf

# Server and shared sources run under Node in Linux images.
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf

# Language starter templates are served verbatim to the editor; their exact bytes
# are compared against user content to decide whether a file was modified, so a
# platform-dependent representation would make that comparison platform-dependent.
languages/**/starters/*  text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
